WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.989
The rich get richer, and the poor get poorer.

00:00:02.989 --> 00:00:05.790
The rich getting richer and the poor getting poorer.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.480
The poor get poorer?

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:12.040
People keep talking about the evil of income inequality.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.000
This is the living room

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.929
in a sixteen million dollar penthouse apartment.

00:00:15.929 --> 00:00:20.330
It’s true that some rich people have gotten absurdly rich.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.560
But the other claim that they got rich

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.029
while poor people got poorer is just a myth.

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:28.060
As we've increased the number of billionaires

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.080
around the world,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.380
extreme poverty has actually shrunk down.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.180
Former investment banker Carol Roth points out

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.720
that anyone who pays attention knows that

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.540
as the rich got richer, most poor people got richer too.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.160
Worldwide, more than a billion

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.300
people rose out of poverty.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:49.120
Yes, the rich got even richer, but why is that a problem?

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:52.460
Consider poor me and rich me.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.780
Over the past 40 years,

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.220
we rich Americans got 200 percent richer, lucky me!

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:00.300
I got just 32% richer.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.500
I didn’t gain as much as he did,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.820
but I don’t see how I’m hurt.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.420
I’m 32 percent richer!

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.549
And yes, that’s adjusting for inflation.

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:10.660
and it doesn’t even count

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.820
all the cool new stuff innovation gave me.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.740
And here’s another misleading claim:

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.535
The lack of economic mobility

00:01:18.535 --> 00:01:20.329
The lack of economic mobility

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:21.560
Watching the news,

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.600
you’d think people born poor in America

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.560
have little chance to become rich.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.900
A striking lack of economic mobility in America.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.320
It’s true that people with rich parents

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.240
have a big advantage,

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:35.990
but it’s not like Americans are locked in.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.560
Economists at Harvard and Berkeley

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.340
crunched the numbers and found most people born to

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.060
the richest fifth of Americans

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.820
fell out of that bracket within 20 years.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.280
Likewise, most born to the poorest fifth

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.779
climbed to a higher quintile.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.240
Some make it all the way to the top.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.999
One study looking at that top bracket found

00:01:55.999 --> 00:01:58.660
Three out of four Americans will hit that

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.310
top 20% at some point in their lifetime.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:02.580
Three out of four people?

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.220
Yes.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.340
There is the opportunity to have that mobility

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.739
and to make an amazing income in this country.

00:02:07.739 --> 00:02:09.900
You see that if you just look at the billionaires

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.320
on the Forbes richest list.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.420
Most are self-made.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.380
In other words, they didn’t inherit the money,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.180
they created their own fortunes.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.040
But politicians and the media say that inequality

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.319
itself is a huge problem.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.700
Frustrations over income inequality

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.780
There’s an inequality in this country right now

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.760
that is threatening to tear us apart.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.760
It might tear us apart,

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.239
if people come to believe that all inequality is evil.

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:37.950
but why is that true?

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.840
Progressives like to point out that

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.760
Scandinavian countries have much more equal incomes

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.340
than America does

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:46.300
[Afghanistan]

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.380
But incomes are more equal in Afghanistan too.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.780
Incomes tend to be equal when everyone is poor.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.680
Total equality isn’t possible.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.700
[Adele singing]

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.540
Some people are just better singers than others.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.100
[Adele singing]

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.900
The best performer in the country

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.680
The best athletes are just physically different.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.720
[gymnastics cheering]

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.220
There's inequality in everything.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.140
There's inequality in free time.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.209
There's inequality in parents.

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:20.620
I don't have any parents or grandparents.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:23.540
We’re are all so different in so many ways.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.319
I have two kidneys.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:27.000
There are people out there who need one,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.459
don't have one that functions.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:30.460
Should the government be able to take my kidney

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.420
because somebody else needs it?

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.960
How is it not wrong that some people have

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.769
so much more than others?

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:37.790
What's wrong about that?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.660
It's absolutely right.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:39.800
It's unfair.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.120
Life is unfair.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.120
Unfair is good.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.209
Unfair is a feature.

00:03:43.209 --> 00:03:44.550
It's not a bug.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.500
Something to think about next time someone

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.860
tells you that it's government’s job

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.620
to make everyone equal.

